{"format":1,"kind":"pfa","id":"pfa-1982","version":"pfa-1982-00f77991","year":1982,"season":"1982","label":"NFL (computed)","local":false,"source":{"provider":"Pro Football Archives","edition":"The 1982 NFL season, computed","compiler":"Pro Football Archives (the facts: starts, positions, box scores); the overall ours, computed from them and read off Madden NFL 2002 (maddenratings.net)","url":"https://www.profootballarchives.com/1982nfl.html","retrieved":"2026-11-09","method":"computed","rawScale":"value","conversion":"Ours, computed: no game rated this NFL season. Each player's season value (his club's credit, its points per game against the league's to the power 0.25, offence and defence apart, shared out: the offensive line by starts; quarterbacks, backs, receivers and tight ends by production, rushing and receiving yards, 0.2 a passing yard, 40 a touchdown and less 60 an interception thrown, and by starts; defenders two thirds by starts and one third by plays, 2 a sack where recorded, 1.5 an interception, 1 a fumble recovered, 1 a return touchdown; kickers by field goals, extra points and accuracy against the league) is ranked among the league-season's players at his game position (ties by starts, then games played) and read off Madden NFL 2002's overalls at that position (the 2001 season: maddenratings.net's 31 team spreadsheets, punters left out), as many of each Madden team's best as the season carries per club, by linear interpolation; rounded and held to 1–99. Then each club moves toward its results: its target is T = μ + √r × S ÷ m, where S is its Simple Rating System (its margins by least squares with a home edge, the NFL's ratings summing to nought) from the season's 126 games, r = 0.428 their reliability, m = 1.808 points of margin a game for each point of the strength the match model plays (its lineup's offence and defence, their mean), measured over 160,000 simulated games under the season's rules, and μ = 78.84 the clubs' mean strength before the move. Every player of a club moves by one whole number and its best few by one more, held to 1–99 and never past a teammate rated above him, whichever brings the club nearest its target: −4 to +4 points this season. The results count twice, by design: the credit's points for and against place a club's players at their positions and weigh its offence against its defence, and the move then sets the club's level from its margins, wherever the credit left it. Facts from Pro Football Archives; the weights tuned once on 2001–2005 against the next season's Madden launch ratings, then frozen."},"map":"nfl1982","clubs":[{"id":"nfl-new-york-jets","name":"New York Jets","code":"NYJ","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 295)","str":82,"squad":[["Richard Todd","QB",89],["Pat Ryan","QB",66],["Freeman McNeil","RB",94],["Mike Augustyniak","RB",83],["Wesley Walker","WR",92],["Lam Jones","WR",75],["Derrick Gaffney","WR",70],["Bobby Jones","WR",61],["Jerome Barkum","TE",75],["Mickey Shuler","TE",69],["Chris Ward","OL",90],["Dan Alexander","OL",90],["Joe Fields","OL",90],["Stan Waldemore","OL",90],["Marvin Powell","OL",76],["John Roman","OL",61],["Joe Pellegrini","OL",57],["Mark Gastineau","DL",91],["Kenny Neil","DL",80],["Abdul Salaam","DL",77],["Marty Lyons","DL",72],["Ben Rudolph","DL",68],["Joe Klecko","DL",68],["Lance Mehl","LB",82],["Greg Buttle","LB",69],["Stan Blinka","LB",69],["Bobby Jackson","CB",99],["Jerry Holmes","CB",81],["Johnny Lynn","CB",66],["Kirk Springs","CB",65],["Darrol Ray","S",84],["Ken Schroy","S",78],["Jesse Johnson","S",57],["Pat Leahy","K",77]]},{"id":"nfl-miami-dolphins","name":"Miami Dolphins","code":"MIA","league":"NFL","country":"840","col":"oklch(0.72 0.16 61)","str":81.9,"squad":[["David Woodley","QB",85],["Don Strock","QB",61],["Andra Franklin","RB",96],["Tony Nathan","RB",83],["Jimmy Cefalo","WR",83],["Duriel Harris","WR",80],["Nat Moore","WR",67],["Vince Heflin","WR",55],["Bruce Hardy","TE",72],["Ronnie Lee","TE",71],["Bob Kuechenberg"